From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kc <barteo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 06:52:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep incremental caches in memory between runs

A daemon that runs KSP again on the same caches directory decoded the
symbols, sealed and sourceToOutputs maps from JSON on every run, wrote
all three back whether or not they had changed (sourceToOutputs twice),
and opened both lookup storages and closed them again.

PersistentMap now keeps each map as last read or written in this
process, with its file's size, modification time and identity: a later
run gets a copy of it while the file still matches, and a map equal to
that copy is not written again. The lookup storages are checked out of
a process-wide pool and put back, open and flushed, at the end of a
run; one is used again only while none of its files has changed since,
and a run that ends with an error closes its storages.
